<b>1st Floor</b>

07:15.200 --> 07:15.370
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:15.200 --> 07:15.370
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:15.370 --> 07:15.490
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:15.370 --> 07:15.490
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:15.370 --> 07:15.490
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:15.490 --> 07:15.530
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:15.490 --> 07:15.530
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:15.530 --> 07:15.580
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:15.530 --> 07:15.580
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:15.580 --> 07:15.620
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:16.330 --> 07:21.050
Now we can use my Dungeon Walk 
to transport the rest of you there.

07:19.410 --> 07:20.370
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:19.410 --> 07:20.370
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:19.410 --> 07:20.370
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:20.370 --> 07:21.250
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:20.370 --> 07:21.250
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:20.370 --> 07:21.250
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:21.050 --> 07:22.970
Thanks, Lily.

07:21.250 --> 07:21.790
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:21.250 --> 07:21.790
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:21.250 --> 07:21.790
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:21.790 --> 07:22.210
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:21.790 --> 07:22.210
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:21.790 --> 07:22.210
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:22.210 --> 07:22.620
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:22.210 --> 07:22.620
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:22.210 --> 07:22.620
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:22.620 --> 07:29.010
<b>1st Floor</b>

07:22.620 --> 07:29.010
<b>45th Floor</b>

07:22.620 --> 07:29.010
<b>49th Floor</b>

07:22.970 --> 07:29.010
No problem. I chose not to go to the 50th floor 
so we could gauge monster frequency.

07:29.570 --> 07:32.400
I've been gathering 
a lot of information, too.

07:32.400 --> 07:35.970
First, I looked into the party compositions 
the two major clans used on their raids.

07:36.290 --> 07:40.180
The Black Dragon Fang took 
four attackers, including their leader,

07:40.180 --> 07:42.440
and two healers for support.

07:43.150 --> 07:47.110
The White Tiger Claw took 
four magic attackers and two healers.

07:47.110 --> 07:50.080
In other words, both clans 
used speed-focused compositions.

07:50.080 --> 07:53.160
So their attackers functioned as tanks, huh?

07:53.680 --> 07:57.990
Also, every floor has a lot of monsters
 that inflict status effects.

07:57.990 --> 08:02.210
<b>Healthy Body</b>

07:57.990 --> 08:02.210
<b>Numbness</b>

07:57.990 --> 08:02.210
<b>Poison</b>

07:57.990 --> 08:02.210
<b>Paralysis</b>

07:58.340 --> 08:02.210
In that case, my Healthy Body skill 
should be able to nullify all that.

08:02.720 --> 08:05.170
It sounds like a challenging labyrinth.

08:05.620 --> 08:08.750
But we have to do whatever it takes 
to clear at least the 51st floor,

08:08.750 --> 08:11.510
and form an alliance 
with the two major clans.

08:12.110 --> 08:13.100
Yeah!

08:15.480 --> 08:18.580
I'll lead. Marius, you bring up the rear.

08:18.580 --> 08:19.390
Sure.

08:20.040 --> 08:21.600
Luna, it's melee for you.

08:21.600 --> 08:24.170
Lilia, adapt to the situation like usual.

08:25.430 --> 08:28.360
Nin, you're on healing. 
Be ready to accept commands from...

08:29.460 --> 08:31.020
Wh-What is it, Lily?

08:31.020 --> 08:32.150
Um...

08:32.150 --> 08:36.110
Could I issue commands during battle?

08:37.520 --> 08:40.580
<i>She's already trying to change.</i>

08:41.240 --> 08:45.730
Okay. If anything, commands from the 
back line will be easiest to understand.

08:46.260 --> 08:49.370
Lily, you're in charge. Nin, assist her.

08:49.370 --> 08:50.420
Got it.

08:50.930 --> 08:53.050
We're all counting on you, Lily.

08:53.500 --> 08:54.550
Right!

08:56.580 --> 08:58.240
Okay, here we go.

08:58.240 --> 08:59.700
Dungeon Walk.

09:04.670 --> 09:08.510
<i>This space isn't suitable 
for speed-focused fighters,</i>

09:08.510 --> 09:11.830
<i>but it could be convenient for me as a tank.</i>

09:12.310 --> 09:14.740
There are monsters positioned nearby.

09:16.040 --> 09:17.520
You're right.

09:17.520 --> 09:18.830
Rud, you can tell, too?

09:18.830 --> 09:20.830
Yeah, more or less.

09:20.830 --> 09:25.020
That's because you're the manager 
of the Avancia Labyrinth.

09:25.020 --> 09:26.670
What? Is that why?

09:27.480 --> 09:29.800
Either way, they've been 
positioned effectively.

09:31.130 --> 09:40.890
<b>Adventurers</b>

09:31.130 --> 09:52.860
<b>Spawn Point</b>

09:31.380 --> 09:39.860
The left and right paths lead to the 
same place, but monsters appear on both.

09:39.860 --> 09:42.160
So if you fight on the left path,

09:42.160 --> 09:46.180
the monsters on the right path
will come up behind you.

09:46.180 --> 09:48.450
Like a pincer movement.

09:48.450 --> 09:52.860
That's right. We might be 
dealing with a tricky guardian.

09:58.030 --> 09:59.420
A poison lizard!

10:00.230 --> 10:02.080
There's a black owl on our right!

10:03.160 --> 10:04.540
Shield of Sacrifice!

10:05.030 --> 10:06.000
Provoke!

10:10.700 --> 10:11.460
A poisonous mist?

10:16.250 --> 10:17.450
Sorry.

10:20.720 --> 10:22.890
But I'm immune to status effects.

10:30.310 --> 10:31.650
<i>Did it use magic to block?</i>

10:47.600 --> 10:49.300
Another black owl!

10:50.500 --> 10:51.440
Rud.

10:51.920 --> 10:55.650
We could defeat them, 
but there's no need for us to keep fighting.

10:55.650 --> 10:56.340
You're right.

10:56.940 --> 11:00.260
The rest of you go on ahead.
 Let me handle this.

11:00.260 --> 11:01.010
Right!

11:01.010 --> 11:02.590
This way, everyone.

11:04.850 --> 11:06.850
Flashing magic stone.

11:13.330 --> 11:16.400
You make a good commander, Lily.

11:16.400 --> 11:17.730
Your orders were clear.

11:18.160 --> 11:20.250
I'll do my best after our break, too.

11:22.480 --> 11:26.720
By the way, I noticed earlier 
that we can decide whether or not

11:26.720 --> 11:30.390
to let you absorb our damage 
using your Shield of Sacrifice.

11:30.390 --> 11:31.060
What?

11:31.060 --> 11:32.850
Yes, she's right.

11:32.850 --> 11:34.790
But we couldn't before.

11:35.200 --> 11:39.400
Maybe your skills were strengthened 
by your battle against me.

11:39.400 --> 11:40.630
Maybe.

11:41.020 --> 11:43.910
Sweet! Then, you have me to thank for that.

11:43.910 --> 11:49.220
Now we can dispel the effect ourselves 
when we don't want you to take our damage.

11:49.560 --> 11:52.540
Either way, your abilities are exceptional.

11:52.540 --> 11:53.590
What?

11:53.590 --> 11:58.440
Few tanks can perfectly draw 
the attention of monsters.

11:58.780 --> 11:59.830
You're right.

11:59.830 --> 12:05.130
I thought most tanks could do that, 
but I guess Rud is just amazing.

12:05.130 --> 12:06.910
I don't know what to say.

12:07.420 --> 12:12.480
It'd be great if you 
learned the Self Heal skill.

12:12.480 --> 12:15.170
You're raising the bar again.

12:15.170 --> 12:16.920
Is there a skill like that?

12:17.220 --> 12:19.630
What's this? Humans don't know about it?

12:20.070 --> 12:24.010
"Humans"? Wait, you mean you're not human?

12:24.010 --> 12:27.470
What? Well, uh, no, I'm not.

12:27.820 --> 12:30.560
Come to think of it, 
we don't know much about you.

12:30.970 --> 12:31.970
You're right.

12:31.970 --> 12:34.640
We once risked our lives fighting you,

12:34.640 --> 12:37.100
but now, you're not a threat to us at all.

12:37.100 --> 12:38.770
We completely forgot to ask.

12:39.330 --> 12:43.250
Marius, could you tell us about yourself?

12:43.250 --> 12:46.240
You don't have to say
anything you don't want to.

12:49.800 --> 12:52.660
I'm not sure if you'll accept it, but...

12:54.210 --> 12:55.150
I'm...

12:56.390 --> 12:57.580
a demonoid.

13:02.930 --> 13:03.880
A demonoid?

13:04.570 --> 13:05.340
Yeah.

13:05.850 --> 13:10.350
Broadly speaking, the creatures of our world 
are divided into humans and demihumans.

13:10.350 --> 13:13.450
Long ago, there were demonoids as well.

13:13.450 --> 13:18.310
Demonoids and demihumans look similar, 
but those who swore loyalty to a demon

13:18.310 --> 13:21.820
instead of the god worshipped by humans
were known as demonoids.

13:22.270 --> 13:24.560
That's the simple version, anyway.

13:25.220 --> 13:28.040
I'm able to manage a labyrinth 
because I'm a demonoid.

13:28.040 --> 13:29.580
What do you mean?

13:29.580 --> 13:30.530
You don't know?

13:31.490 --> 13:35.030
Currently, humans use them 
for their own benefit,

13:35.030 --> 13:40.540
but labyrinths were originally created 
by a demon to destroy the world of humans.

13:40.540 --> 13:41.500
What?

13:41.920 --> 13:47.580
You mean our god <i>didn't</i> create 
the labyrinths to enrich our lives?

13:47.580 --> 13:50.160
Where did that story come from?

13:51.280 --> 13:53.570
It's what we've been told
 for generations, I guess.

13:53.570 --> 13:59.060
Right. Although, perhaps 
someone once knew the truth.

13:59.480 --> 14:01.850
Well, now you know.

14:01.850 --> 14:05.090
A demonoid probably 
manages this labyrinth, too.

14:05.090 --> 14:07.100
A pretty strong one at that.

14:08.170 --> 14:12.240
So you should be careful
 when you fight the guardian.

14:12.240 --> 14:18.750
Sure, but aren't demonoids your people? 
Are you okay with fighting one?

14:19.370 --> 14:23.600
I don't like them. If this is what
 they're doing with their lives,

14:23.600 --> 14:28.220
then I will defeat them not 
as a demonoid, but as Marius.

14:28.220 --> 14:29.440
I see.

14:29.440 --> 14:35.680
Forgive me. I accompanied your raid 
so I could fight a personal battle.

14:37.990 --> 14:41.740
At the very least, 
I think of you as a friend.

14:41.740 --> 14:44.110
I appreciate your continued support.

14:46.090 --> 14:49.840
As long as you don't hurt Lily,
 I have no complaints.

14:49.840 --> 14:52.980
I'll pretend we never
 had this conversation.

14:52.980 --> 14:57.090
So will I. As long as you don't 
hurt my sister, we can be friends.

14:57.090 --> 15:01.040
That's all you two care about, isn't it?
 Not that I disagree.

15:01.040 --> 15:02.040
Same here.

15:02.440 --> 15:03.580
Good for you.

15:04.480 --> 15:07.460
It's all because of you. Thank you, Rud.

15:08.000 --> 15:09.920
Um, excuse me.

15:09.920 --> 15:10.550
Lily?

15:10.820 --> 15:13.890
I'm sorry to ruin the mood,

15:13.890 --> 15:20.600
but I'd like to discuss how we'll fight the 
monsters confirmed to be on the 50th floor.

15:22.010 --> 15:23.560
Got it. Go ahead.

15:23.840 --> 15:25.020
Right!

15:27.440 --> 15:31.200
First, there are the lizards. 
We can use an orthodox approach to...

15:33.660 --> 15:38.080
<i>We progressed through the labyrinth,
defeating every monster in front of us.</i>

15:39.070 --> 15:41.290
<i>And at last, we reached the 50th floor.</i>

15:52.450 --> 15:54.720
It's a bone dragon.

15:55.080 --> 15:56.180
Let's go, guys!

15:56.930 --> 15:58.140
Provoke!

16:00.000 --> 16:01.900
<i>My Provoke's working well.</i>

16:01.900 --> 16:04.430
<i>We'll be able to use Lily's strategy.</i>

16:04.900 --> 16:15.450
Bone wings

16:04.900 --> 16:15.450
Made entirely of bones

16:04.900 --> 16:15.450
Four legs

16:04.900 --> 16:15.450
Long tail

16:05.550 --> 16:10.450
We've confirmed that there are 
bone dragons on the 50th floor.

16:10.450 --> 16:17.470
They frequently cause status effects, 
which could disrupt our formation.

16:18.720 --> 16:24.710
So we'll get Rud to charge in first while the
 rest of us stay out of range of its attacks.

16:25.110 --> 16:26.380
Got it.

16:26.380 --> 16:30.050
My sister and Marius will attack
 from outside its range.

16:30.050 --> 16:35.030
Since it's a bone monster, it's better to 
use crushing rather than slashing attacks.

16:35.030 --> 16:35.890
Okay.

16:35.890 --> 16:36.550
Sure.

16:36.980 --> 16:44.480
Also, since it's weak to fire, we should enchant 
our weapons with fire before taking one on.

16:44.480 --> 16:46.150
And primarily use fire magic, too.

16:46.570 --> 16:51.410
Plus, once a bone dragon loses a
 certain amount of health, its body...

17:00.910 --> 17:01.910
Rud!

17:04.700 --> 17:06.160
Thanks, Lily.

17:06.160 --> 17:06.830
Sure thing.

17:06.830 --> 17:09.320
<i>We should avoid standing under its wings.</i>

17:09.320 --> 17:12.710
<i>I'll draw its attention 
some more before moving.</i>

17:16.860 --> 17:17.880
Master!

17:18.760 --> 17:23.600
It's okay, Luna. He's allowing 
himself to get knocked back.

17:24.090 --> 17:26.080
<i>It's quicker than I expected,</i>

17:26.080 --> 17:28.690
<i>and I've gotten a bit too 
far away from the others.</i>

17:32.130 --> 17:33.760
Thanks, you two.

17:33.760 --> 17:35.900
I was just itching to hit something.

17:35.900 --> 17:37.680
Okay, let's keep this up.

17:37.680 --> 17:38.450
Yeah!

17:39.910 --> 17:42.370
<i>Each one of its attacks is quick and heavy,</i>

17:42.370 --> 17:45.750
<i>but as long as I watch closely 
and brace myself, it's not a problem.</i>

17:47.650 --> 17:48.370
What is that?

17:50.710 --> 17:51.920
An AOE attack?

17:54.920 --> 17:56.110
Is everyone okay?

17:56.110 --> 18:00.470
I only suffered a scratch, but I seem to be 
afflicted with some type of poison effect.

18:00.470 --> 18:01.260
Me, too.

18:01.820 --> 18:04.700
Nin, cure them while I distract the enemy.

18:04.700 --> 18:07.790
Got it. Let's heal them, Luna.

18:07.790 --> 18:08.600
Okay.

18:11.060 --> 18:12.020
Take this!

18:13.280 --> 18:15.750
We know you're weak to fire!

18:17.570 --> 18:18.780
Provoke!

18:19.610 --> 18:21.280
What? It just...

18:21.280 --> 18:25.370
<i>So after suffering several attacks, 
it ignores my Provoke and attacks randomly.</i>

18:25.760 --> 18:27.460
Rud, brace for an attack!

18:30.280 --> 18:32.000
My shoulder's gonna dislocate.

18:34.620 --> 18:36.880
<i>My shield feels heavy.</i>

18:36.880 --> 18:38.220
<i>What is this sludge?</i>

18:38.750 --> 18:41.720
Someone hit me with a water spell. 
This sludge is sticking—

18:43.840 --> 18:46.140
The sludge is making my shield too heavy.

18:46.400 --> 18:47.340
Rud!

18:50.560 --> 18:52.130
Thanks, Nin.

18:52.130 --> 18:56.990
This is looking like it'll be a long battle,
 which means I should...

18:59.360 --> 18:59.950
What's that?

19:00.520 --> 19:02.320
It's an auto-healing area.

19:02.320 --> 19:06.830
It's a saint skill that's only available to Nin: 
an area that allows absorb shield recovery.

19:08.230 --> 19:11.410
It's up and running. Make good use of it.

19:11.410 --> 19:12.080
Got it.

19:12.080 --> 19:16.670
<b>1 Hour Later</b>

19:12.130 --> 19:16.670
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

19:14.720 --> 19:16.670
<i>It still won't go down?</i>

19:17.660 --> 19:18.130
What now?

19:20.590 --> 19:22.300
Lily warned us about this.

19:25.780 --> 19:28.520
The flames are coming. 
Get out of the way, everyone.

19:29.300 --> 19:30.270
Rud?

19:37.100 --> 19:38.000
Rud!

19:38.000 --> 19:38.740
Master!

19:42.420 --> 19:45.030
Why do you look so surprised?

19:45.030 --> 19:48.040
Did you think I'd be burnt to a crisp?

19:49.040 --> 19:50.080
Provoke!

19:57.440 --> 20:00.970
That barrage of attacks dealt about 
5,000 damage to my absorb shield.

20:00.970 --> 20:02.050
This isn't good.

20:04.470 --> 20:06.660
You got me good earlier.

20:06.660 --> 20:08.560
It's time I took you out.

20:13.390 --> 20:14.150
Now!

20:16.250 --> 20:19.080
It's working. Just a little more.

20:20.110 --> 20:21.610
Provoke!

20:21.610 --> 20:24.240
Thank you, Rud.

20:26.550 --> 20:30.750
<i>This isn't the end of our journey!</i>

20:34.270 --> 20:37.500
Life Conversion!

20:44.880 --> 20:48.310
Those are the bone dragon's 
materials. It's over.

20:49.680 --> 20:52.390
Congratulations on 
clearing the 50th floor.

20:52.800 --> 20:53.940
Thanks.

20:55.190 --> 21:01.790
But surely you don't intend to immediately
 go and raid the 51st floor, right?

21:01.790 --> 21:04.820
No. That's enough for today.

21:08.430 --> 21:13.830
Rud, I think we should wait a little while 
to sell the materials we gathered today.

21:13.830 --> 21:17.510
Word would get out that we've been
 making progress on our raid.

21:17.510 --> 21:21.210
You're right. We can sell everything later.

21:21.480 --> 21:24.160
Lily, even back in town, 
your commands are spot on.

21:24.160 --> 21:25.880
Oh, um...

21:27.780 --> 21:30.280
I'll do my best on the next floor, too.

21:30.280 --> 21:33.650
Then, it's time for the customary after-party!

21:33.650 --> 21:34.580
Yeah!

21:35.260 --> 21:37.050
Sorry. I can't today.

21:38.930 --> 21:42.170
I'm a little tired. 
I want to head back early and rest.

21:43.900 --> 21:45.360
Then, I will, too.

21:47.050 --> 21:48.980
See you all tomorrow.
